      '**Third: Face your demons.** The difficult energies in your psyche — cravings, rage, shame, fear — need to be acknowledged, not suppressed. Instead of going to war with your demons, invite them to tea. Say: "I see you. What do you need?" Often they just need to be acknowledged. What you resist persists. What you acknowledge begins to release its grip.',
      "**Fourth: Seek guidance from mentors.** You can't do this alone. You need coaches, sponsors, therapists, wise friends — people who've walked this path before you, who can see your blind spots. Regularly seek guidance. Be teachable. Let others help you. Humility isn't weakness. It's the willingness to receive what you cannot give yourself.",
