      "**Recovery principles** are the accumulated wisdom of countless people who have walked this road before you — distilled into principles, slogans, steps, and practices. They don't replace your own discernment, but they provide a tested framework that your addicted brain cannot generate on its own. When in doubt, return to the principles.",
      '**Community** is the group of people who share your commitment to recovery — who see you, who will call you out, who will celebrate with you, who will sit with you in the hard times. The research on recovery consistently shows that social connection is among the most protective factors for long-term recovery. Isolation kills. Community heals.',
