      'Self-pity is seductive. "Poor me. Look how hard my life is. Nobody understands. I\'ve had it worse than everyone. I deserve to be bitter." Self-pity feels like self-compassion, but it\'s not. Self-compassion acknowledges suffering and responds with kindness. Self-pity wallows in suffering and uses it as an excuse.',
