      "Yes, you've been through hard things. Yes, you've suffered. Yes, life has been unfair. AND dwelling on it doesn't help. It hurts. There is a difference between acknowledging pain and performing it. Acknowledging pain: \"I've been through something genuinely hard, and it has affected me, and I'm doing the work to heal.\" Wallowing in pain: \"I've been through something hard, and that's why nothing is my fault, and why I don't have to try.\" The Way teaches: \"Forget the former things; do not dwell on the past. See, I am doing a new thing!\"",
